      "text": "Just as with the sine function, the values of the sine function repeat after every 2π, or 360°.\nTherefore, we can add or subtract multiples of 2π to find equivalent angles.\nWe have $\\frac{11 \\pi}{3} = 3\\pi + \\frac{2 \\pi}{3} \\approx \\frac{10 \\cdot 2 \\pi}{3} + \\frac{2 \\pi}{3}$.\nTherefore, $\\sin \\frac{11 \\pi}{3} = \\sin \\frac{2 \\pi}{3} = \\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}}$.\nThe answer is: \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}",
